WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
unjam: see inside your Slurm job. Live, on every node.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:11.900
Your 4-node job is slow. Which node? Which process?

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.200
unjam --slurm starts one small agent per node in an overlap step.

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.500
Each agent reads the cgroup v2 tree and streams it back. No daemon, no root.

5
00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:24.570
unjam --slurm: all nodes of job 4242 in one tree

6
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.153
node3 lags: 14 % CPU, the other nodes 90 %

7
00:00:29.153 --> 00:00:31.201
v: step, node or flat layout

8
00:00:31.201 --> 00:00:36.579
flat: every process, sorted by CPU

9
00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:39.567
/: filter by name or path

10
00:00:39.584 --> 00:00:44.742
unjam: any cgroup v2 host: slices, services, sessions

11
00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:48.633
Enter: every metric of one process

12
00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:51.883
unjam record writes one Arrow file per node.

13
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:55.133
Replay it later with unjam --replay, or read it with pyarrow.

14
00:00:55.151 --> 00:01:02.700
unjam --replay: scrub through a recorded job

15
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:11.000
Install with mise or dnf. Documentation: gsi-hpc.github.io/unjam

